#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:43
#: b269ce3c4361468f92d7df78b2af45e7
msgid "The system is composed of 4 ETH connectors available for the connection of external systems. They are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:45
#: 3ced540563644a8f8b835591055f64c6
msgid "**ETH 0 – VIDEO:** This is the only ETH port for payload connection. It is not connected to the ETH Switch, but directly to the data link. Normally, this port would be connected to the payload control laptop or PC. This port does not have POE (Power Over Ethernet)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:46
#: cf365b734e2b4cb191d8a8a94c1715de
msgid "**ETH 2 & 4 – CS/JY:** Port for the connection of the control station laptop or UAV control Joystick. This port does have POE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:47
#: 27edb282896546c19b319c9f08ed7493
msgid "**ETH 5 – IMU & GNSSCOMPASS:** This port is reserved for the connection of the IMU & GNSSCOMPASS module. This port does have POE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:55
#: e57fb72e81bc4fcaafbf84dbddea2b28
msgid "Data Link Interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:57
#: 71338129e0934a1581a988870bab9eb3
msgid "The system has available two redundant datalinks which once configured can connect automatically to the airborne datalinks, using one at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:59
#: b61bec9f4d0a439eb6fc197c5c21fe96
msgid "One datalink of 900MHz is placed internally into the VTA and transfers only telemetry information to the tracking system, while the other datalink of a wide range of available frequencies (2.4-5.8 GHz) is externally placed into the Pan Tilt Unit (PTU) and transfers telemetry information and video through the external port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:61
#: 48e4b206ca1c4f8f9330d5fc1afbb7e5
msgid "The following diagram shows the pinout of the PTU used to connect and power data links. This is to be used only for custom data link integrations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:74
#: 4fa3f54c629742baa3faba71c1d6a894
msgid "Telemetry is transferred through serial interface to the internal tracking controller, which selects automatically the active link and transfers the information to the PC through the HUB port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:77
#: 8f7d686fdf5744f9ba6c850ad9fce847
msgid "Data output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:79
#: 382358843f5347d3a01ee9e80eb40471
msgid "The VTA main processing unit has its own proprietary ICD to feed other systems (C2 or UAV ground control software) with its status information. This information can be streamed in parallel with other streams like NMEA 0183/NMEA 2000 output or the GNSS and compass IMU information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:83
#: 18bf8f04f35944eb9890bfebda3ff75a
msgid "More information about the specific communications protocol (ICD) can be requested from `Alpha Unmanned Systems <https://alphaunmannedsystems.com/contact/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:86
#: 1679c3676d784d48b251d8cab197fbf4
msgid "VCS Installation and integration on vessels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:88
#: 93cb6a890d074c91bd2852b1e281de39
msgid "Vessels are equipped with a variety of RF equipment, typically including radars and satcom devices. As they may interfere with the communications between the VTA and the UAV, there are some general rules for finding a good spot for installation on the vessel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:90
#: c791b973155f4608813c1fff7648d72e
msgid "VTA antennas or secondary radios must be as far as possible from the radar and, if possible, in a different horizontal plane to avoid being under the RF interference of the radar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:91
#: fc23c3ef5305489bbb0fbf48ae16b106
msgid "The GNSS compass and IMU must have a clear view of the sky to correctly receive the signal from GNSS satellites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:92
#: 1fe2d8ee83a04b279737a1616a45c2c0
msgid "If some area between the VTA and the UAV’s flight zone would be shadowed by the vessel’s mast or any other vessel structure, this can be solved by installing the 900MHz antenna or secondary radio systems and antennas at a different location. A schematic overview of potential locations can be found below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:99
#: 0300ba8092e1423c8cbec6fb3107ee12
msgid "BLUE circles represent potential spots for the installation of the main VTA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:100
#: 14c1e5332f67446a8357b3a32ed6fe56
msgid "RED circles represent the potential installation points of the 900 MHz antennas, secondary radio or secondary VTA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:101
#: b23a17ddcd0243c2b5f6c81d3b32196b
msgid "BLUE lines are ETH cables to be routed from one system to the other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:104
#: c53bf4d376c244a18487a5fa7f08dc23
msgid "Integration steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:106
#: 473ea621246e4fc1b0387596706daa06
msgid "**Antenna location definition:** based on line of sight and RF compatibility with other systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:107
#: 32d436f894e5413aa17e1ca41858d0d2
msgid "**Operators location definition:** the permanent location for the operator must be defined taking into consideration that EP will require visual access to the UAV during take-off and landing. Operators room must be able to accommodate 2 operators with 2 laptops and it is desirable to have extra screens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:108
#: b62d77768e3743718f0bcd32ad6fed48
msgid "**Antenna Interface definition:** interface between antenna and vessel is defined. Normally it will be a mast with a plate on top matching the holes pattern of the base of the VCS antennas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:109
#: 3dbb07ab2fc441629eda6bbaaf8b6f66
msgid "**Distances:** lengths between all the components (antenna, center of heli-deck and operators room) must be defined. These lengths will be used to define reference offsets and to manufacture the cables with the appropriate measure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:112
#: b6e33d7b83a849dcbfe6030702c40794
msgid "Vessel Based Tracking Antenna Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:114
#: c38cf350a85d4993991418b340a7b6c7
msgid "The tracking antenna has the following requirements that must be taken into consideration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:116
#: 050b58917d16432db882e339b89a0ce2
msgid "**Power supply:** the antenna utilizes 220 V AC power supply; it can include a 24V DC backup power source but normally on a vessel the AC power source would be integrated with a UPS system. From the control room, the power supply of the VTA must be able be switched on and off by means of a switch as the ON/OFF button of the system will not be accessible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-alphaunmannedsystems-vcs.rst:117
#: 33d1fdec6fc8447ea08fbcda41b80b06
msgid "**Cables routing:** 2 ETH cables and one power supply cable must be routed from the antenna to the operator’s room. One more ETH cable must be routed from the antenna to the flight deck for the control joystick of the external pilot."
msgstr ""

